gned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{1/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186503893 :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[2]{{x}^{9}}={x}^{9/2}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{9}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[2]{{x}^{9}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{9/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{9/2+1}}{(\\frac{9}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{11/2}}{(\\frac{11}{2})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{11/2}}{11}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{11/2}}{11}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{11/2}}{11})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{11}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{11/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{11}\\cdot \\frac{11}{2}{x}^{11/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{9/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[2]{{x}^{9}}={x}^{9/2}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{9}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[2]{{x}^{9}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{9/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{9/2+1}}{(\\frac{9}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{11/2}}{\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{11/2}}{11}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{11/2}}{11}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{11/2}}{11}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{11}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{11/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{11}\\cdot \\frac{11}{2}{x}^{11/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{9/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186503894 :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as 